\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My song is love unknown;
\par My Saviour's love to me;
\par Love to the loveless shown,
\par That they might lovely be
\par O who am I 
\par That for my sake,
\par My Lord should take
\par Frail flesh, and die?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He came from His blest Throne,
\par Salvation to bestow;
\par But men dame strange, and none
\par The longed-for Christ would know.
\par But O my Friend
\par My Friend indeed,
\par Who at my need
\par His life did spend.
\par \pard\fi720 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Sometimes they strew His way,
\par And His sweet praises sing;
\par Resounding all the day,
\par Hosannas to their King.
\par Then: Crucify
\par Is all their breath,
\par And for His death
\par They thirst and cry.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Why, what hath my Lord done?
\par What makes this rage and spite?
\par He made the lame to run,
\par He gave the blind their sight.
\par Sweet injuries!
\par Yet they at these
\par Themselves displease,
\par And against Him rise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. They rise and needs will have
\par My dear Lord made away;
\par A murderer they save;
\par The Prince of life they slay.
\par Yet cheerful He
\par To suffering goes
\par That He His foes
\par From thence might free.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. In life, no house, no home
\par My Lord on earth might have
\par In death, no friendly tomb
\par But what a stranger gave.
\par What may I say?
\par Heav'n was His home
\par But mine the tomb
\par Wherein Him lay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Here might I stay and sing,
\par No story so divine;
\par Never was love, dear King,
\par Never was grief like Thine.
\par This is my Friend,
\par In whose sweet praise
\par I all my days
\par Could gladly spend.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

